'''Lindsay Clarke''' ({{nee|Meyer}}; born September 23, 1988) is an American rower. She was born in [[Seattle, Washington|Seattle]], [[Washington (state)|Washington]]. She competed at the [[2008 Summer Olympics]] in Beijing, where she placed fifth in [[Rowing at the 2008 Summer Olympics – Women's quadruple sculls|quadruple sculls]], together with [[Lia Pernell]], Jennifer Kaido and [[Margot Shumway]].<ref name="sref">{{cite Sports-Reference |title=Lindsay Meyer |url=https://www.sports-reference.com/olympics/athletes/me/lindsay-meyer-1.html |accessdate=August 12, 2012}}</ref><ref>{{citation|url=http://www.row2k.com/features/405/row2k-Interview---Lindsay-Meyer/|title=Interview: Lindsay Meyer|author=Erik Dresser|work=row2k.com|date=March 4, 2009|accessdate=July 14, 2016}}</ref>

==Professional athletics career==
<!-- ===South Jersey Rowing Club=== -->

===Cooper Junior Rowing Club===
Lindsay is currently one of the two head coaches at the Cooper Junior Rowing Club,<ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-06-28 |title=Coaches |url=https://cooperjrs.demosphere-secure.com/about-mrc/coaches |access-date=2025-09-17 |website=Cooper Junior Rowing Club}}</ref> the aggregate successor club to her former club, the South Jersey Rowing Club, and the Moorestown Rowing club.

