'''Oriol Cardona Coll''' (born 7 October 1994) is a Spanish [[Ski mountaineering|ski mountaineer]] and [[Skyrunning|skyrunner]]. He represented Spain at the [[2026 Winter Olympics]] and won a gold medal in the [[Ski mountaineering at the 2026 Winter Olympics – Men's sprint|sprint race]], the first gold medal for Spain at the [[Winter Olympic Games]] since [[1972 Winter Olympics|1972]].

==Career==
Cardona made his [[European Championships of Ski Mountaineering|European Championships]] debut in 2022 and won a gold medal in the sprint race with a time of 3:17.988.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.insidethegames.biz/articles/1119047/ismf-cardona-coll-jagercikova |title=Cardona Coll and Jagerčíková win sprint titles on first day of ISMF European Championships |website=[[insidethegames.biz]] |first=Patrick |last=Burke |date=9 February 2022 |access-date=29 December 2025}}</ref> He then competed at the [[2023 World Championship of Ski Mountaineering]] and won a gold medal in the sprint race with a time of 2:35.218.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.insidethegames.biz/articles/1134263/ski-mo-sprint-world-champs |title=Delight for first time champions in sprint events at Ski Mountaineering World Championships |website=[[insidethegames.biz]] |first=Philip |last=Barker |date=28 February 2023 |access-date=29 December 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.mundodeportivo.com/deportes-invierno/20230228/1001952646/oriol-cardona-proclama-campeon-mundial-esprint.html |title=Oriol Cardona, campeón del mundo de sprint |website=mundodeportivo.com |date=28 February 2023 |access-date=29 December 2025 |language=Spanish}}</ref> He again competed at the 2024 European Championships and won a gold medal in the mixed relay along with [[Ana Alonso Rodriguez]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://ismf-ski.com/oriol-cardona-and-ana-alonso-soar-to-victory-at-the-mixed-relay-european-championships/ |title=Oriol Cardona and Ana Alonso soar to victory at the Mixed Relay European Championships |website=ismf-ski.com |date=12 January 2024 |access-date=29 December 2025}}</ref>

On 26 January 2025, during the first mixed relay of the season, he won a gold medal with a time of 30:23.6.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://ismf-ski.com/the-spanish-duo-ana-alonso-rodriguez-and-oriol-cardonna-coll-win-the-first-mixed-relay-of-the-season/ |title=The Spanish duo Ana Alonso Rodriguez and Oriol Cardonna Coll win the first Mixed Relay of the season. |website=imsf-ski.com |date=26 January 2025 |access-date=29 December 2025}}</ref> He finished the [[2024–25 ISMF Ski Mountaineering World Cup]] reaching the podium in all five relay events, including three golds and two silvers, to win the mixed relay World Cup title with 480 points. He also finished first in the men's sprint World Cup standings with 575 points.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://fedme.es/ana-alonso-y-oriol-cardona-aseguran-el-titulo-de-la-copa-del-mundo-de-relevos-mixtos-con-victoria-en-villars/ |title=Ana Alonso y Oriol Cardona aseguran el título de la Copa del Mundo de Relevos Mixtos con victoria en Villars. |website=fedme.es |date=5 April 2025 |access-date=29 December 2025 |language=Spanish}}</ref>

He again competed at the [[2025 World Championship of Ski Mountaineering]] and won a gold medal in the sprint race with a time of 2:45.40.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.olympics.com/en/milano-cortina-2026/news/2025-ismf-ski-mountaineering-world-championships-marianne-fatton-oriol-cardona-coll-claim-sprint-world-titles-in-morgins-secure-milano-cortina-2026-quota-spots |title=2025 ISMF Ski Mountaineering World Championships: Marianne Fatton and Oriol Cardona Coll claim sprint world titles in Morgins, secure Milano Cortina 2026 quota spots |website=olympics.com |first=Nischal |last=Schwager-Patel |date=6 March 2025 |access-date=29 December 2025}}</ref> With the win, Spain earned a quota spot for the discipline at the [[2026 Winter Olympics]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://as.com/masdeporte/polideportivo/el-ano-de-oriol-cardona-aspirante-a-todo-en-los-juegos-de-invierno-f202601-n/ |title=El año de Oriol Cardona: aspirante a todo en los Juegos de Invierno |newspaper=[[Diario AS]] |first=Jorge |last=Noguera |date=4 January 2026 |access-date=4 January 2026 |language=Spanish}}</ref> He also won a silver medal in the mixed relay, along with Rodriguez, with a time of 32:45.0, losing to France's team of [[Emily Harrop]] and [[Thibault Anselmet]] by 0.9 seconds.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.olympics.com/en/milano-cortina-2026/news/2025-ismf-ski-mountaineering-world-championships-france-spain-quota-spots-milano-cortina-2026/ |title=2025 ISMF Ski Mountaineering World Championships: France and Spain finish 1-2 in mixed relay to secure quota spots Milano Cortina 2026 |website=olympics.com |first=Chloe |last=Merrell |date=3 March 2025 |access-date=29 December 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.insidethegames.biz/articles/1152265/first-skimo-spots-awarded-for-2026-games |title=First skimo 2026 spots awarded |website=[[insidethegames.biz]] |first=Elliot |last=McGowan |date=11 March 2025 |access-date=29 December 2025}}</ref> He earned a scholarship for the 2026 Winter Olympics.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.insidethegames.biz/articles/1153640/celebrating-olympic-scholarship-success |title=Celebrating Olympic scholarship success |website=[[insidethegames.biz]] |first=Gretelle |last=Jimenez |date=2 June 2025 |access-date=29 December 2025}}</ref>

On 19 February 2026, Cardona won the first-ever men's Olympic gold medal in [[Ski mountaineering at the Winter Olympics|ski mountaineering]], finishing in first place in the [[Ski mountaineering at the 2026 Winter Olympics – Men's sprint|sprint race]] with a time of 2:34.03.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.catalannews.com/sports/item/oriol-cardona-makes-history-as-first-man-to-win-olympic-ski-mountaineering-gold |title=Oriol Cardona makes history as first man to win Olympic ski mountaineering gold |publisher=[[Catalan News Agency]] |date=19 February 2026 |access-date=19 February 2026 |language=Spanish}}</ref> This marked Spain's first Winter Olympic gold medal since [[1972 Winter Olympics|1972]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.olympics.com/en/milano-cortina-2026/news/winter-olympics-2026-oriol-cardona-coll-wins-historic-first-olympic-men-s-ski-mountaineering-sprint-gold |title=Winter Olympics 2026: Oriol Cardona Coll wins historic first Olympic men's ski mountaineering sprint gold |website=olympics.com |first=Will |last=Imbo |date=19 February 2026 |access-date=19 February 2026}}</ref> On 21 February 2026, he won a bronze medal in the [[Ski mountaineering at the 2026 Winter Olympics – Mixed relay|mixed relay]], along with Alonso, with a time of 27:23.94.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://en.ara.cat/sports/oriol-cardona-and-ana-alonso-win-the-bronze-medal-in-the-relay-race_1_5655357.html |title=Oriol Cardona and Ana Allonso win the bronze medal in the relay race |website=en.ara.cat |first=Toni |last=Padilla |date=21 February 2026 |access-date=21 February 2026}}</ref>

== Personal life ==
Since 2023, he has been in a relationship with actress [[Amaia Aberasturi]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.elmundo.es/loc/famosos/2026/02/19/6996dd1ee85ece3f278b457b.html |title=Oriol Cardona y su discreta relación con la actriz Amaia Aberasturi: nominada al Goya, fan de la naturaleza... |date=19 February 2026 |access-date=21 February 2026 |newspaper=[[El Mundo (Spain)|El Mundo]] |language=es}}</ref>

