'''Luiz Henrique Eloy Amado''' (born February 2, 1988), better known as '''Eloy Terena''', is a Brazilian lawyer, [[anthropologist]], researcher, [[professor]], and an indigenous leader of the [[Terena people|Terena]] ethnic group, whose work is primarily focused on the defense of the [[Indigenous rights|rights]] of [[indigenous peoples in Brazil]]. Since January 2023, he has served as Executive Secretary of the [[Ministry of Indigenous Peoples (Brazil)|Ministry of Indigenous Peoples]], and on March 31, 2026, he was sworn in as Minister, succeeding [[Sônia Guajajara]].

== Biography ==
Eloy Terena was born in the Ipegue indigenous village, in the municipality of [[Aquidauana]], [[Mato Grosso do Sul]], on February 2, 1988. Following his parents' separation in 1991, his mother began working as a domestic housemaid in [[Campo Grande]], where he moved with his siblings to live with her. Influenced by his sister, he decided to study Law and was awarded a full scholarship through the [[Programa Universidade para Todos|Programa Universidade Para Todos]] (ProUni) to attend the [[Dom Bosco Catholic University]], from which he graduated.<ref name="com.br">{{Cite web |last=Minas |first=Estado de |date=2020-08-08 |title=Eloy Terena: o advogado que marcou o 'direito indígena' |url=https://www.em.com.br/app/noticia/politica/2020/08/08/interna_politica,1174379/eloy-terena-o-advogado-que-marcou-o-direito-indigena.shtml |access-date=2026-07-18 |website=[[Estado de Minas]] |language=pt-BR}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mineo |first=Liz |date=2022-10-20 |title=Brazilian Indigenous lawyer talks about fight for Native rights |url=https://news.harvard.edu/gazette/story/2022/10/brazilian-indigenous-lawyer-talks-about-fight-for-native-rights/ |access-date=2026-07-18 |website=[[Harvard Gazette]] |language=en-US}}</ref> Encouraged by his professor Antônio Brandi, he came into contact with the struggles of indigenous peoples and developed a growing interest in [[indigenous rights]]. At the same university, he earned a master's degree in Local Development.<ref name="com.br"/>

From 2012 onward, when he became a member of the Special Commission for the Defense of the Rights of Indigenous Peoples of the Federal Council of the [[Order of Attorneys of Brazil]] (OAB),<ref name="puc-rio">{{Cite web |title=Aula inaugural com Luis Eloy Terena – Departamento de Direito da PUC-Rio |url=https://www.jur.puc-rio.br/aula-inaugural-com-luis-eloy-terena/ |access-date=2026-07-18 |language=pt-BR}}</ref> Terena began providing legal counsel to various indigenous communities and [[Indigenism|indigenist]] organizations,<ref name="exame">{{Cite web |title=Advogado Terena lidera defesa das causas indígenas no país |url=https://exame.com/brasil/advogado-terena-lidera-defesa-das-causas-indigenas-no-pais/ |access-date=2026-07-18 |website=Exame |language=pt-br}}</ref> organizing training courses for leadership development,<ref name="cimi">{{Cite web |last=cimi |date=2015-09-30 |title=Famasul e Acrissul contra um advogado Terena no MS: "Querem nos intimidar usando todo poder que têm no estado" {{!}} Cimi |url=https://cimi.org.br/2015/09/37750/ |access-date=2026-07-18 |language=pt-BR}}</ref> and advocating on behalf of indigenous causes before the [[Supreme Federal Court]]. One of his greatest achievements was securing the reversal of a judicial decision that had expelled several communities from the traditional lands they had reoccupied in 2013.<ref name="exame"/> This, however, led to persecution on the part of [[União Democrática Ruralista|ruralist]] organizations, which challenged the veracity of his indigenous identity and called for the suspension of his master's degree.<ref name="cimi"/><ref>{{Cite web |title=Pedido para cassar advogado terena é "impertinente", diz OAB |url=https://correiodoestado.com.br/cidades/pedido-de-comissao-para-cassar-advogado-terena-e-impertinente-diz-o/259638/ |access-date=2026-07-18 |website=correiodoestado.com.br |language=pt-BR}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=cimi |date=2015-10-09 |title=Carta da Fian em solidariedade aos advogados Rogério Batalha e Luiz Henrique Eloy Terena {{!}} Cimi |url=https://cimi.org.br/2015/10/37812/ |access-date=2026-07-18 |language=pt-BR}}</ref>

In 2022, he obtained a doctorate in Sociology and Law from the [[Fluminense Federal University]], with the thesis ''The Social Field of Law and the Theory of Indigenist Law'',<ref name="pucpr">{{Cite web |title=Luiz Eloy Terena |url=https://www.pucpr.br/escola-de-direito/docente/luiz-eloy-terena/ |website=Pontifícia Universidade Católica do Paraná}}</ref> and completed a postdoctoral fellowship in Social Sciences at the [[School for Advanced Studies in the Social Sciences]] in Paris.<ref name="pucpr"/> He became responsible for the filing of a {{Interlanguage link|Claim of non-compliance with a fundamental precept|lt=claim of non-compliance with a fundamental precept|pt|Arguição de descumprimento de preceito fundamental}} (ADPF) that led the Supreme Federal Court to mandate that the [[Presidency of Jair Bolsonaro|Bolsonaro administration]] adopt protective measures for indigenous peoples against the [[COVID-19]]. This marked the first time that an indigenous lawyer prevailed in a constitutional jurisdiction action before that Court.<ref name="com.br"/>

In 2022, he joined the transition team of then-president-elect [[Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva]], representing the state of Mato Grosso do Sul on the Technical Group for Indigenous Peoples,<ref>{{Cite web |title=Eloy Terena é escolhido para assumir Ministério dos Povos Indígenas |url=https://www.opantaneiro.com.br/politica/eloy-terena-e-oficialmente-escolhido-para-assumir-ministerio-dos-povos/188950/ |access-date=2026-07-18 |website=www.opantaneiro.com.br}}</ref> and was subsequently nominated for the position of Executive Secretary of the Ministry of Indigenous Peoples, assuming office in January 2023.<ref name="puc-rio"/> Following Minister [[Sônia Guajajara]]'s resignation from office to qualify for the [[2026 Brazilian general election|2026 elections]], President Lula confirmed that Eloy Terena would take over the Ministry,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Rodrigues |first=Basília |date=2026-03-27 |title=Lula confirma Eloy Terena no ministério dos Povos Indígenas e Rivetla Édipo na Pesca {{!}} Coluna da Basília {{!}} SBT News |url=https://sbtnews.sbt.com.br/colunas/coluna-da-basilia/lula-confirma-eloy-terena-no-ministerio-dos-povos-indigenas-e-rivetla-edipo-na-pesca |access-date=2026-07-18 |website=sbtnews.sbt.com.br |language=pt-br}}</ref> and he was sworn in on March 31, 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-03-31 |title=Guajajara passa chefia do ministério dos Povos Indígenas a Eloy Terena |url=https://www.cnnbrasil.com.br/politica/guajajara-passa-chefia-do-ministerio-dos-povos-indigenas-a-eloy-terena/ |access-date=2026-07-18 |website=CNN Brasil |language=pt-BR}}</ref>

